             ,HELPFUL HINTS

,FOR EVERYONE3 ,A WAY TO REMEMBER3 A
  ROOT GROWS UNDER THE GROUND4 ,CARROTS1
  RADISHES1 TURNIPS AND SWEET POTATOES
  ARE DUG OUT OF THE SOIL4
,VISION3 ,HOLD A REAL CARROT1 RADISH AND
  TURNIP4 ,GET TO KNOW THEM BY FEELING
  THEIR SHAPE AND SMELLING THEM3 THE
  CARROT AND THE RADISH ARE LONG1 AND
  THE TURNIP IS ROUND4
,MOVEMENT3 ,IF MOVING A PENCIL ROUND THE
  LEAF IS HARD1 PUT THE LEAF UNDER THE
  PAPER AND RUB A THICK CRAYON OVER IT1
  OR LET A PARTNER HOLD THE LEAF STILL4
,FOR TEACHERS3 ,BRING REAL CARROTS1
  RADISHES AND TURNIPS1 WITH THEIR
  LEAVES1 TO CLASS SO THAT CHILDREN CAN
  SEE THAT THE PART WE EAT IS BELOW THE
  LEAVES3 IT IS THE ROOT4 ,WHEN
  COLLECTING LEAVES1 PAIR CHILDREN WHO
  USE A WHEELCHAIR OR HAVE LOW VISION
  WITH A BUDDY1 AND LET EVERY CHILD
  CHOOSE AT LEAST ONE LEAF THEMSELVES4

